body:
The MCP `organize` door names its path closure `rel` and does not relativise, so it emits absolute filesystem paths into a JSON payload whose field names promise project-relative ones.

`intent-cli/src/mcp.rs:1446`:

    let rel = |paths: &[std::path::PathBuf]| -> Vec<String> {
      paths.iter().map(|p| p.display().to_string()).collect()
    };

It feeds `hydrated`, `rewritten`, `unchanged`, `dehydrated`, `unclaimed`, `diverged` and `pruned` in the door's answer.

**THE SAME FILE CARRIES TWO CORRECT SPELLINGS OF THE SAME CLOSURE**, in the `st hydrate` and `st dehydrate` doors, and both call through the one home:

    let rel = |paths: &[std::path::PathBuf]| -> Vec<String> {
      paths.iter().map(|p| f.project().relative(p)).collect()
    };

So this is one wrong closure between two correct ones, in one file, under the same name. Every other `rel` over a path vector in the tree calls `project.relative` -- `facade.rs:6073` (the `disk.organize` event), `facade.rs:8475` (`ViewWork`), `facade.rs:8808`, and the two neighbours above.

**WHY THE NAME IS PART OF THE DEFECT RATHER THAN A COSMETIC COMPLAINT.** A closure called `rel` whose body does not relativise reads as correct at every call site, because the call sites are `rel(&report.hydrated)` and say nothing about what `rel` does. The next person to add a field to this payload will call `rel` and get absolute paths under a relative-sounding key, which is how a single site becomes a class.

**CONSEQUENCE.** An MCP consumer of `organize` receives paths carrying the operator's home directory and the project's location, which are neither portable between machines nor comparable against anything the CLI prints for the same run -- `render.rs` relativises the same vectors for display. Two doors onto one act answer differently about what a path is.

**SCOPE, STATED BECAUSE IT IS WHY THIS IS NOT FOLDED INTO 0509.** Changing it changes an outward JSON contract that consumers may already depend on, which is a different blast radius from an internal digest and needs a record a consumer can find by searching for the behaviour it saw. 0509 is the digest inside `intentsvcs`; this is the wire.

**NOT A CASE FOR MAKING `Report` RELATIVE**, which was measured against and refused under 0509: two consumers act on those paths as real filesystem locations (`prune_emptied`'s `starts_with(root)` filter, and the `wrote` filter against absolute `owned` in `facade.rs:6472`), and relativising the report would break both silently while type-checking. The report is absolute correctly; the DISPLAY and the WIRE are what relativise, and this door is the wire.

**PROVENANCE.** Found by cc on 2026-09-22 while censusing `Report`'s consumers for issue 0509, and filed by vc after driving the three anchors directly. Neither the defect nor its two correct siblings were reached by any test.
